# BEGINNER NOTE:
# [Android App Signing & Keystore Protection]
# Android requires all applications to be digitally signed with a cryptographic certificate
# before installation or upload to Google Play.
# - The Java KeyStore (.jks) contains the private key used to sign APKs and App Bundles.
# - This example template illustrates the format of `android/key.properties`.
# SECURITY CRITICAL:
# Never commit `key.properties` or any `.jks`/`.keystore` file to version control.
# If a private signing key is leaked or lost, existing users cannot receive updates securely.
# In CI/CD, signing keys should be stored in encrypted GitHub Secrets or KMS.
#
# Copy to android/key.properties and replace every placeholder locally.
# Never commit key.properties or the keystore.
storeFile=/absolute/path/to/paper-route-upload.jks
storePassword=REPLACE_LOCALLY
keyAlias=paper-route-upload
keyPassword=REPLACE_LOCALLY
